            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "Middleware redirects logged-out users away from /dashboard. A `deletePost(id)` Server Action has no session check. Can a logged-out user delete a post?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "Yes. Actions are public POST endpoints, so they can be called directly.",
                "Middleware is only an optimistic, path-based gate.",
                "Fix: call `verifySession()` and check ownership inside the action."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "An admin bans a user. With a 7-day JWT cookie versus a database session, who is locked out on the next request?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "Database session: locked out at once, because the row is deleted.",
                "JWT cookie: still valid until expiry, because verification is only a signature check.",
                "So keep JWTs short-lived."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "The auth check sits only in `layout.tsx`. A user client-navigates between two pages under it. What is the bug?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "Layouts do not re-render on client navigation, so the check can be skipped.",
                "Check in every page or in the data fetch.",
                "Best: put it in the DAL function."
              ],
              "example_code": [
                "const post = await getPost(id)"
              ]
            }
